    "id": "madas/alevel-applied-c/q1",
    "question": "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-c/q1-question-1.svg\" alt=\"A B 7 5 1 24 24 24 11 24 The figure above shows the probability sample space for two events A and B , summarized by a Venn diagram.\" style=\"--madas-width:558.7px\"></figure><figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-c/q1-question-2.svg\" alt=\"Determine the following probabilities. a) At least one of the events A , B occurs. ( ) 1 b) At most one of the events A , B occurs. ( ) 1 c) Only event B occurs. ( ) 1 ( ) d) Exactly one of the events A , B occurs. 1 e) None of the events A , B occurs. ( ) 1 f) Either both events occur or neither event occurs. ( ) 1\" style=\"--madas-width:570.7px\"></figure><figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-c/q1-question-3.svg\" alt=\"g) Either event A occurs or neither event occurs. ( ) 1 The word “or” in this question only implies one event or the other but not both.\" style=\"--madas-width:569.3px\"></figure>",
    "steps": [
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-c/q1-solution-1.svg\" alt=\"Read the four disjoint regions in the Venn diagram: Their probabilities are 7/24 for A only, 5/24 for both events, 1/24 for B only and 11/24 for neither: (a) P(A ∪B) counts all three interior regions: At least one means all the regions in the union: (7 + 5 + 1)/24 = 13/24 . [A1]\" style=\"--madas-width:677.3px\"></figure>",
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-c/q1-solution-2.svg\" alt=\"(b) The disjoint events A ∩B′, B ∩A′, A′ ∩B′ give (7 + 1 + 11)/24 = 19/24. Equivalently, at most one excludes the intersection: 1 −5/24 = 19/24 . [A1] (c) For B ∩A′, the B-only region is 1/24 . [A1] (d) The event (A ∩B′) ∪(A′ ∩B) contains two disjoint regions: Exactly one means either single-set region: (7 + 1)/24 = 1/3 . [A1] (e) For A′ ∩B′, the region outside both sets is 11/24 . [A1] (f) For (A ∩B) ∪(A′ ∩B′), add the intersection and the region outside both: (5 + 11)/24 = 2/3 . [A1] (g) The event A ∪(A′ ∩B′) = A ∪B′.\" style=\"--madas-width:677.3px\"></figure>",
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-c/q1-solution-3.svg\" alt=\"Add all of A and the region outside both sets: (7 + 5 + 11)/24 = 23/24 . [A1]\" style=\"--madas-width:677.3px\"></figure>",
      "<p class=\"madas-total\">Total mark for question 1 is 7 marks.</p>"
    ],
    "promptText": "A B 7 5 1 24 24 24 11 24 The figure above shows the probability sample space for two events A and B , summarized by a Venn diagram. Determine the following probabilities. a) At least one of the events A , B occurs. ( ) 1 b) At most one of the events A , B occurs. ( ) 1 c) Only event B occurs. ( ) 1 ( ) d) Exactly one of the events A , B occurs. 1 e) None of the events A , B occurs. ( ) 1 f) Either both events occur or neither event occurs. ( ) 1 g) Either event A occurs or neither event occurs. ( ) 1 The word “or” in this question only implies one event or the other but not both."
  },
