    "question": "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-c/q8-question-1.svg\" alt=\"The discrete random variable X has the following probability distribution x 0 1 3 1 1 1 P X ( = x ) 6 3 2 Two independent observations of X are made, denoted by X and X . 1 2 a) Find the probability distribution of X + X . ( ) 5 1 2 b) Calculate P X ( &gt; X ) . ( ) 3 1 2\" style=\"--madas-width:572.0px\"></figure><figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-c/q8-question-2.svg\" alt=\"Question diagram\" style=\"--madas-width:581.3px\"></figure>",
    "steps": [
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-c/q8-solution-1.svg\" alt=\"(a) Multiply the probabilities for independent observations, using both orders for unequal values. In ascending order of the sum, the six calculations are (1/6)2, 2(1/6)(1/3), (1/3)2, 2(1/6)(1/2), 2(1/3)(1/2), and (1/2)2. [B1] [A1] Sum 0 1 2 3 4 6 Ordered outcomes (0, 0) (0, 1), (1, 0) (1, 1) (0, 3), (3, 0) (1, 3), (3, 1) (3, 3) 1 1 1 1 1 1 Probability 36 9 9 6 3 4 [M1] [M1] [A1] (b) The ordered pairs with X1 &gt; X2 are (1, 0), (3, 0), (3, 1). Their disjoint probabilities sum to\" style=\"--madas-width:642.7px\"></figure>",
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-c/q8-solution-2.svg\" alt=\"(1/3)(1/6) + (1/2)(1/6) + (1/2)(1/3) = 1/18 + 1/12 + 1/6 . = 11/36 As a check, the probabilities of X1 &gt; X2 and X2 &gt; X1 [B1] are equal by symmetry: [A1] Equality has probability 1/36 + 1/9 + 1/4 = 14/36, so P(X1 &gt; X2) = 1 1 −14 = 11   36 . [A1] 2 36\" style=\"--madas-width:678.7px\"></figure>",
      "<p class=\"madas-total\">Total mark for question 8 is 8 marks.</p>"
    ],
