  {
    "id": "madas/alevel-applied-c/q9",
    "question": "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-c/q9-question-1.svg\" alt=\"100 N 60° 25kg The figure above shows a small box of mass 25 kg , pulled along rough horizontal ground by a light inextensible rope, which is inclined at 60° to the horizontal. The force supplied by the rope is 100 N .\" style=\"--madas-width:561.3px\"></figure><figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-c/q9-question-2.svg\" alt=\"The box, which is modelled as a particle, is in limiting equilibrium. Calculate the value of the coefficient of friction between the box and the ground. ( ) 5\" style=\"--madas-width:574.7px\"></figure>",
    "steps": [
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-c/q9-solution-1.svg\" alt=\"Let R be the normal reaction and F be the friction force. [M1] Equilibrium vertically gives R + 100 sin 60◦= 25g. [A1] Horizontal equilibrium gives F = 100 cos 60◦. [A1] At limiting equilibrium F = µR, [A1] hence R = 25g −100 sin 60◦.\" style=\"--madas-width:677.3px\"></figure>",
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-c/q9-solution-2.svg\" alt=\"Substituting into the horizontal equation gives µ(25g −100 sin 60◦) = 100 cos 60◦, so 100 cos 60◦ µ = 25g −100 sin 60◦≈0.316 . [A1]\" style=\"--madas-width:677.3px\"></figure>",
      "<p class=\"madas-total\">Total mark for question 9 is 5 marks.</p>"
    ],
    "promptText": "100 N 60° 25kg The figure above shows a small box of mass 25 kg , pulled along rough horizontal ground by a light inextensible rope, which is inclined at 60° to the horizontal. The force supplied by the rope is 100 N . The box, which is modelled as a particle, is in limiting equilibrium. Calculate the value of the coefficient of friction between the box and the ground. ( ) 5"
  },
