      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-c/q11-solution-2.svg\" alt=\"Take upwards as positive, with acceleration −g. (a) For P, u = 17.5, a = −9.8, s = −H, t = 5. Using s = ut + 1 2at2, the displacement after 5 seconds is −H = 17.5(5) −1 2(9.8)(5)2 = 87.5 −122.5 = −35, H = 35 m . [M1] Choose a consistent signed displacement [M1] use the initial vertical velocity [A1] include the gravitational term [A1] evaluate the positive height (b) At impact P’s velocity is 17.5 −9.8(5) = −31.5 m s−1, [M1] so V = 31.5. [A1] Then Q’s impact speed is 6V/7 = 27 m s−1. [A1] Using v2 = u2 + 2as [A1] for Q, (−6V/7)2 = 36 49(31.5)2 = 272 = U2 + 2(−9.8)(−35) = U2 + 686, Subtract 686 and take the positive square root, giving √ √ U = 729 −686 = 43 ≈6.56 . [M1] [A1]\" style=\"--madas-width:678.7px\"></figure>",
      "<p class=\"madas-total\">Total mark for question 11 is 10 marks.</p>"
    ],
