    "question": "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-c/q12-question-1.svg\" alt=\"Relative to a fixed origin O , the horizontal unit vectors i and j are pointing due east and due north, respectively. A ship A is moving with constant velocity. At noon A is at the point with position vector ( 12 i + 12 j km and at 2 p.m. it has ) sailed to the point with position vector ( 8 i + 20 j km . ) a) Determine the velocity of A . ( ) 3 b) Write down an expression for the position vector of A , t hours after noon. ( ) 2 A ship B is also moving with constant velocity and its position vector, r km , t hours after noon is given by\" style=\"--madas-width:573.3px\"></figure><figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-c/q12-question-2.svg\" alt=\"r = ( 2 t + k ) i + ( 2 t + 33 ) j, where k is a scalar constant. c) Given that A intercepts B determine the value of k . ( ) 3\" style=\"--madas-width:578.7px\"></figure>",
    "steps": [
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-c/q12-solution-1.svg\" alt=\"(a) With r = r0 + vt, 8i + 20j = 12i + 12j + 2v. Subtract the initial position: In two hours the displacement of A is −4i + 8j kilometres: [B1] Its velocity is (−2i + 4j) km h−1 . [M1] [A1] (b) At time t, r = (12i + 12j) + (−2i + 4j)t. The position of A is (12 −2t)i + (12 + 4t)j [A1] kilometres: [A1]\" style=\"--madas-width:677.3px\"></figure>",
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-c/q12-solution-2.svg\" alt=\"(c) At the interception the north components are equal: 12 + 4t = 2t + 33, [M1] hence 2t = 21, so t = 10.5. The east components satisfy 12 −2t = 2t + k, [A1] giving k = 12 −4t = 12 −42, or k = −30 . [A1]\" style=\"--madas-width:680.0px\"></figure>",
      "<p class=\"madas-total\">Total mark for question 12 is 8 marks.</p>"
