      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-c/q13-solution-1.svg\" alt=\"(a) From a = 6t −18, integration gives Z (6t −18) dt = 3t2 −18t + C. v =\" style=\"--madas-width:466.7px\"></figure>",
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-c/q13-solution-2.svg\" alt=\"Initially 15 = 0 −0 + C, so C = 15. Integrate the acceleration and use v(0) = 15: [M1] [A1] v(t) = 3t2 −18t + 15 [M1] [M1] [A1] = 3(t −1)(t −5). At rest 0 = 3t2 −18t + 15, hence 0 = t2 −6t + 5 = (t −1)(t −5). The rest times are t = 1 s and t = 5 s . [M1] [A1] (b) An antiderivative is Z (3t2 −18t + 15) dt = t3 −9t2 + 15t + D. x = At t = 0, x = 0, giving D = 0.\" style=\"--madas-width:677.3px\"></figure>",
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-c/q13-solution-3.svg\" alt=\"Integrate the velocity and use x(0) = 0, [M1] giving x(t) = t3 −9t2 + 15t. Evaluating the two positions gives 1 −9 + 15 = 7 and 125 −225 + 75 = −25. Thus x(1) = 7 m [A1] and x(5) = −25 m. [A1] The distance between the positions is 32 m . [A1] Equivalently, the velocity stays non-positive from t = 1 to t = 5, [A1] so the integral is [t3 −9t2 + 15t]5 1 = (125 −225 + 75) −(1 −9 + 15) = −25 −7 . = −32 Thus the magnitude of the signed area under the velocity curve is Z 5 = 32 m. v(t) dt [A1] 1\" style=\"--madas-width:677.3px\"></figure>",
      "<p class=\"madas-total\">Total mark for question 13 is 13 marks.</p>"
    ],
